## 2. Strain-isolation cores and sandwich

| ID | Material | Where | Why |
|---|---|---|---|
| HEMP-W | Degummed hemp bast, woven 2×2 or 4×4 | Plate cores, harness skin cores | SIP analog, damping, mass |
| HEMP-U | Hemp unidirectional tape | Directed-stress skins on cores | Bearing along principal stress |
| HEMP-M | Short-fiber hemp mat / oriented hurd | Core fill | Bulk, insulation |
| MAT-P | Phenolic or polyimide matrix (flight-like) | Hemp impregnation | Temp + outgas vs epoxy |
| MAT-E | Toughened epoxy | Ground demo only | Not a flight core matrix |
| ADH-F | High-temp flexible adhesive (RTV-class or space-rated equivalent) | Ceramic IML ↔ core ↔ backing | Strain isolation bondline 0.15–0.25 mm |
| SEAL-PI | PI tape + resin dam | All hemp core edges | Stop vacuum / moisture wick |
| SKIP | — | Inside sternum cup, inside hatch ring bore | Hemp is forbidden in the cup |

Incoming hemp: moisture bake-out, bag with desiccant. Treat like prepreg.

